<section id="gems" class="lp-anchor">
  <div class="lp-section-head centered">
    <span class="eyebrow lp-eyebrow">The gems</span>
    <h2 class="no-top-margin">Free, and free forever.</h2>
    <p class="paragraph m secondary">
      Four MIT gems with no usage limits. Take the framework alone, or add the dashboard, persistence
      and tracing for apps that call models another way.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="lp-grid two">
    <div class="lp-card">
      <h3><span class="lp-glyph accent">@</span><a href="https://github.com/activeagents/activeagent" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">activeagent</a></h3>
      <p class="paragraph s secondary">
        The framework. Agents, actions and prompt templates; ten providers; tools, schema tools, MCP servers
        and delegation; structured output and streaming; evaluations and telemetry built in.
      </p>
      <div class="lp-node-foot">
        <span class="lp-chip">gem "activeagent"</span>
        <span class="lp-chip">rails g active_agent:install</span>
      </div>
      <a class="lp-docs" href="https://docs.activeagents.ai/framework" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">docs/framework -&gt;</a>
    </div>

    <div class="lp-card">
      <h3><span class="lp-glyph accent">-&gt;</span><a href="https://github.com/activeagents/activeagent/tree/main/actionagent" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">actionagent</a></h3>
      <p class="paragraph s secondary">
        The dashboard, as a mountable Rails engine. Traces, metrics, interactions and evaluations; the agent
        builder, versions and the Run Agent workbench; your agents served as an MCP server. Prebuilt assets,
        no JavaScript build in your app.
      </p>
      <div class="lp-node-foot">
        <span class="lp-chip">gem "actionagent"</span>
        <span class="lp-chip">rails g action_agent:install</span>
      </div>
      <a class="lp-docs" href="https://docs.activeagents.ai/framework/dashboard" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">docs/dashboard -&gt;</a>
    </div>

    <div class="lp-card">
      <h3><span class="lp-glyph accent">#</span><a href="https://github.com/activeagents/solid_agent" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">solid_agent</a></h3>
      <p class="paragraph s secondary">
        Persistence as models you own. Conversation context, agent-curated long-term memory, durable runs
        with progress events, tool result caching, model pricing, and portable agent manifests
        (<code class="lp-inline-code">.agent.md</code>, dotprompt, CrewAI).
      </p>
      <div class="lp-node-foot">
        <span class="lp-chip">gem "solid_agent"</span>
        <span class="lp-chip">rails g solid_agent:install</span>
      </div>
      <a class="lp-docs" href="https://docs.activeagents.ai/solid_agent" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">docs/solid_agent -&gt;</a>
    </div>

    <div class="lp-card">
      <h3><span class="lp-glyph accent">~</span><a href="https://github.com/activeagents/activeagents-telemetry" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">activeagents-telemetry</a></h3>
      <p class="paragraph s secondary">
        Tracing for Ruby apps that call models without the framework. The RubyLLM adapter reports every chat
        turn as a trace on the same wire format, to a mounted dashboard or the platform. Bodies are sent only
        when you say so.
      </p>
      <div class="lp-node-foot">
        <span class="lp-chip">gem "activeagents-telemetry-ruby_llm"</span>
      </div>
      <a class="lp-docs" href="https://docs.activeagents.ai/framework/ruby_llm_dashboard" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">docs/ruby_llm_dashboard -&gt;</a>
    </div>

    <div class="lp-card wide">
      <h3><span class="lp-glyph accent">+</span>Need it hosted?</h3>
      <p class="paragraph s secondary">
        The platform at <a href="https://activeagents.ai">activeagents.ai</a> runs the same dashboard for a team:
        workspaces and seats, retention and quotas by plan, published evaluation reports from CI, managed
        sandboxes and support. Every workspace starts with a free trial, and your app only needs the framework gem.
      </p>
      <div class="button-group">
        <a class="button tertiary" href="https://activeagents.ai">Explore the platform</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
